<title>UK: Biotechnology NAV recovers in 1996.</title>
<headline>Biotechnology NAV recovers in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biotechnology Investments Ltd said on Tuesday that net asset value (NAV) per share rose to 6.17 dollars at November 30, 1996 compared with 4.65 a year earlier.</p>
<p>The specialist biotech investment company said in a statement that NAV per share recovered from a low point in July 1996 to stand at $6.62 by December 31, 1.4 percent higher than the NAV at May 31.</p>
<p>The company said that net asset value on November 30 was $342.6 million versus $257.9 million previously.</p>
<p>It said a total of $29 million was invested in biotech companies worldwide including three new private companies in the U.S. and one each in France, Israel and the UK.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
